+// Negative impls are unstable syntax, which the compiler rejects (as a
+// future-incompatibility warning for now) even under a disabled `cfg`, so
+// that every build of objc2 warned. The body of a macro is only parsed
+// where the macro is used, so they are written through one that is only
+// used when the feature is enabled.
 #[cfg(feature = "unstable-autoreleasesafe")]
